lisa-design:
- vulns nests osv-scanner-reusable-pr.yml as a job (nesting works: caller -> ci-<kind> -> ci-common -> osv = 4 levels). Its job declares actions:read, contents:read, security-events:write, so every caller of ci-common must grant those (plus pull-requests:read for pr-title). Documented in README.
- vulns upload-sarif is disabled for PRs whose head repo != github.repository (fork tokens are read-only, upload would fail).
- pr-title and vulns run on pull_request only (spec); actionlint runs on every event. actionlint uses setup-go `stable` (callers may not be Go repos) and the same pinned go run actionlint@v1.7.12 as this repo.
- Dedupe uses an Actions cache entry (key = ccf-notify-failure-sha256(repo\0sha\0workflow)), lookup-only before posting and saved after a successful post. Chosen over Slack conversations.history (needs channels:history, scope not known to be granted) and over "an earlier run failed" heuristics (would skip when the earlier post never happened). The key is pinned by a golden test: changing it re-posts already-reported failures.
- For pull_request events the commit is pull_request.head.sha, not GITHUB_SHA (the merge commit changes whenever base moves).
- Rule (b): previous run = latest completed push run of the same workflow_id on the default branch with lower run_number and a decisive conclusion (success/failure/timed_out/startup_failure); cancelled/skipped/neutral/stale are stepped over; no previous run counts as passing. Default branch comes from the event payload, falling back to main.
- notify-failure cannot know the ref it was called at (no job.workflow_sha context), so it checks out compliance-framework/workflows at input workflows-ref (default v1) to build cmd/notify. Callers pinning a SHA/branch must pass the same ref. Alternative (OIDC job_workflow_sha claim) needs id-token: write; rejected.
- The caller decides failure (`if: failure()` on the notify job); the reusable workflow does not re-check the run's result.
- Token gate is a shell step (secrets can't be used in if:); notify post also no-ops on an empty token. A post error or a missing channel fails the notify job (visible), and the marker is not saved, so a re-run retries.
- This repo's ci.yml dogfoods ./.github/workflows/ci-common.yml (replaces its standalone actionlint job), so pr-title/vulns/actionlint run on this PR.

lisa-selfreview:
pass 1 (strict): request_changes.
- [must-fix] CORE-SIZE-001: first draft was ~1500 counted lines (>1000). Trimmed code/tests/README, dropped ci-common inputs and the ci.yml dogfooding; now <1000.
- [must-fix] ci-common.yml vulns: osv-scanner exits before writing results when a repo has no lockfiles (policies, helm), so the reusable workflow's "both scans completed" check would fail every PR there. Fix: scan-args add --allow-no-lockfiles.
- [must-fix] CORE-ID-001 internal/notify DedupeKey: keyed on the workflow *name*, which two workflow files in one repo can share. Fix: key on the workflow file path from GITHUB_WORKFLOW_REF (name as fallback).
- [should-fix] cache-scoped dedupe: a push run on renovate/x and a pull_request run for the same commit save markers in different cache scopes, so a caller triggering on both would post twice. Callers push-trigger on main only; recorded in design notes, not fixed.
